menu "Headset: audio path (modules/hs_audio)"

    config HS_AUDIO_CODEC_RATE_HZ
        int "Codec sample rate (Hz)"
        default 48000
        help
            The rate the codec is clocked for at boot (ADC and DAC alike on the
            AIC3104). Every profile's speaker rate must equal it; the boom
            microphone is decimated from it to the profile's mic rate.

    config HS_AUDIO_MIN_ATTEN_HALF_DB
        int "Hearing-safety cap: minimum DAC attenuation (0.5 dB steps)"
        default 6
        range 0 127
        help
            The host's volume is applied to the codec but never louder than this
            much attenuation below full scale (6 = -3 dB). Set it from a
            measurement of the real drivers at full scale (TBD-018): headphone
            output level depends on driver sensitivity and impedance.

    config HS_AUDIO_INITIAL_ATTEN_HALF_DB
        int "Volume at boot, before the host sets one (0.5 dB steps of attenuation)"
        default 24
        range 0 127

    config HS_AUDIO_BOOM_GAIN_HALF_DB
        int "Boom microphone PGA gain (0.5 dB steps)"
        default 40
        range 0 119
        help
            40 = +20 dB for an electret on 2.5 V MICBIAS through 2.2 k. Tune on
            the first board with the boom actually used.

endmenu
